<title>NEW ZEALAND: Telecom, Samoa agree on cellular network.</title>
<headline>Telecom, Samoa agree on cellular network.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecom Corp of New Zealand said on Tuesday it had signed a joint venture with the Western Samoan government to build a cellular telephone network.</p>
<p>A joint venture, Telecom Samoa Cellular Ltd, would build and operate the network.</p>
<p>A full range of services would be offered. In addition, the government had decided to use the cellular network to provide some rural customers with cellular as a cost effective telephone service.</p>
<p>Services are scheduled for introduction in mid-1997.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
